<title>JAPAN: Japanese net foreign bond buyers in October.</title>
<headline>Japanese net foreign bond buyers in October.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Net purchases of foreign bonds by Japanese investors totalled 1.6741 trillion yen in October after net purchases of 440.1 billion yen a month earlier, the Ministry of Finance (MOF) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Bonds include beneficiary certificates, but exclude all bills.</p>
<p>Net selling of Japanese stocks by foreign investors amounted to 70.3 billion yen in October compared with net purchases of 377.1 billion yen the previous month, the ministry said.  </p>
<p>Details of Japanese and foreigners' investments, in billions of yen, were as follows:</p>
<p>JAPANESE INVESTMENT</p>
<p> Foreign stocks: Net	     Foreign bonds: Net</p>
<p> October     +112.3	     October   +1,674.1</p>
<p> September    +86.0	     September   +440.1</p>
<p>FOREIGNERS' INVESTMENT</p>
<p> Japanese stocks: Net	    Japanese bonds: Net</p>
<p> October	-70.3	     October     +372.5</p>
<p> September   +377.1	     September +1,419.6</p>
<p>Figures are rounded and based on settlements.</p>
</text>
